<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pembroke Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1093">1093</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pembroke Castle is a medieval castle in Pembroke, south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnulf-de-montgomery">Arnulf de Montgomery</a> in 1093. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-marshal-1st-earl-of-pembroke">William Marshal</a> rebuilt it in stone from about 1200, adding its great round keep. It was the birthplace of Henry VII in 1457, and in 1648 it was besieged and taken by Parliamentarian forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell">Oliver Cromwell</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pembroke-castle.jpg" alt="Pembroke Castle" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JKMMX · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pembroke_Castle_-_June_2011.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
